<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Scroll Anytime — iOS shell entitlements.

  The PWABuilder template ships this file declaring aps-environment (push), camera, audio-input,
  location, printing and the macOS app-sandbox keys. Scroll Anytime uses NONE of them. Declaring an
  entitlement the app does not exercise is a Guideline 2.5.4 rejection, and the camera / mic /
  location ones would flatly contradict the privacy answers already filed in App Store Connect.

  What remains earns its place: associated domains, so a shared /c/ or /r/ link opens the app
  instead of Safari; and Sign in with Apple (1.0.2), which the account sheet and the onboarding
  hero offer natively through the shell's `siwa` bridge (SignInWithApple.swift). The site already serves
  /.well-known/apple-app-site-association for those paths; it stays inert until the owner sets
  `apple_app_id` (TEAMID.com.scrollanytime.app) in /admin → Config, so shipping this is safe either
  way.

  ship/ios-lint.sh checks this file against an exact whitelist and fails loudly on anything else.

  aps-environment (2026-09-28): NOT YET. The shell schedules LOCAL notifications (NotifyBridge.swift:
  the daily seder, streak at risk, the weekly recap, come back - all planned from /me/rollup), which
  need no entitlement. Remote pushes (a milestone while the app is closed, a rabbi's new clips) need
  the Push Notifications capability ON the App ID (App Store Connect API bundleIdCapabilities, or the
  developer portal) AND an APNs key in the Worker's secrets (MAC-DAY.md STEP 4.5). Add
      aps-environment = development (as a key/string pair)
  here the moment the capability is on - with it absent the provisioning profile cannot carry the
  entitlement and signing fails on the runner.

  Deliberately ABSENT:
    com.apple.security.device.camera             — no capture anywhere in the product
    com.apple.security.device.audio-input        — same
    com.apple.security.personal-information.location
                                                 — there is no location code in the product at all
    com.apple.security.print                     — nothing is printable
    com.apple.security.app-sandbox / files.*     — macOS keys; meaningless in an iOS app
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.developer.applesignin</key>
	<array>
		<string>Default</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
	<array>
		<string>applinks:scrollanytime.com</string>
		<string>applinks:www.scrollanytime.com</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
